<!DOCTYPE airframe SYSTEM "../airframe.dtd">
<airframe name="Twisty">
  <description>
    Full pivot wing airframe with a Pixracer flightcontroller

    + MODEL:       Kavan Twisty
    + FC:          PX4 FMU 4.0 in the form of a Pixracer v1.0 R15
    + ACTUATORS:   Default regular metal gear 9g servos
    + GNSS:        uBlox M10N
    + MAG:         QMC5883L Magnetometer
    + ESC:         Aria 70A AM32
    + RCRX:        OpenRXSR Receiver
    + AIRSPEED:    None
    + TELEMETRY:   Si10xx Chip based with SiK FlexFreq firmware
    + CURRENT:     A standard V/I alternative to 3DR PowerBrick
    + RANGEFINDER: Surertech VB50A 
    + MOTOR:       Default Kavan C2814-1400 16 Pole Brushless motor
    + PROP:        Default Foldable 2 Blade 7" x 6"

    NOTES:
    + FC Build in with servo pins pointing down, USB port pointing to Tail, see IMU_MPU_CHAN_X Y Z and IMU_MPU_X Y Z_SIGN for correct orientation
    + If one happens to come accross a clone Pixracer R15 with an MPU6500 instead of MPU9250 one can use the MPU6000 IMU module instead
      Important to have IMU_MPU_USE_MEDIAN_FILTER enabled since bad quality MPU6500 chips often exhibit spikes in raw MPU sensor output 
      This MPU6500 has no magnetometer on chip, use an external magnetometer if needed e.g. there is likely one on the GNSS module
    + The Surertech VB50A rangefinder can be used for AGL measurements during deepstall landings
    + For testflights the built in SD card slot on the Pixracer FC to store inflight highspeed data might come in handy to analyze issues
      Enable the logger module when needed...
    + The magnetometer needs to be enabled in the AHRS module to be used for heading estimation when flying spin curve maneuvers
    + UART2 is port Telem1, UART3 is port Telem2 on Pixracer FC
  </description>

